## Deployment
{% if deploy_target == 'render' %}
This app deploys to [Render](https://render.com).
The Render Blueprint in `render.yaml` is the only deploy definition.
It declares the Docker web service `{{ app_name }}`{% if include_db %} and the Postgres database `{{ app_name }}-db`{% endif %}.
Do not create or change these resources by hand in the dashboard.

### First deploy

1. Push this repo to GitHub.
2. Open `https://render.com/deploy?repo=<github-url>`. Replace `<github-url>` with the URL of this repo. You can also use New > Blueprint in the Render dashboard.
3. Read the plans and the monthly cost. Then apply the Blueprint.
4. If no deploy starts, start one manual deploy from the service page.

### After the first deploy

- A change to `render.yaml` merged to `main` syncs to the live services.
- Render deploys a new commit on `main` only after CI passes (`autoDeployTrigger: checksPass`).
{% if include_db %}- `render.yaml` sets `DATABASE_URL` from the `{{ app_name }}-db` database.
- Migrations run as the pre-deploy command: `{{ app_name }}-migrate`. It runs `alembic -c app/db/migrations/alembic.ini upgrade head` with no arguments, because Render drops pre-deploy arguments on Docker services.
- The database accepts no external connections (`ipAllowList: []`). For manual database work, use the Shell tab of the web service in the Render dashboard, or `render ssh`.
{% endif %}{% if include_backend %}{% if auth_provider == 'google' %}- Sign-in uses Google. Protected API routes return 503 `auth_not_configured` until the Google settings are set. `/health` returns 200. See "Google sign-in" for the setup order.
{% else %}- Auth is not configured. This app has no Logto application yet. Protected API routes return 503 `auth_not_configured`, whatever token is sent. `/health` returns 200.
- Register a Logto API resource for this app. Grant the `read` scope to the intended users. Set `LOGTO_ENDPOINT` and `LOGTO_API_RESOURCE` in the Render service environment.
{% if include_frontend %}- Create a Logto single page app for this service. Set its redirect URI to `<service URL>/callback` and its sign-out URI to `<service URL>`. Set `LOGTO_APP_ID` to its client ID. Set `VITE_LOGTO_ENDPOINT`, `VITE_LOGTO_APP_ID`, and `VITE_LOGTO_API_RESOURCE` to the same values as their server settings. Redeploy to rebuild the frontend.
{% endif %}- For machine access, create a separate Logto machine-to-machine client for this app. Grant it the API scopes it needs. Set `LOGTO_M2M_AGENT_APP_ID` and `{{ app_name | replace('-', '_') | upper }}_M2M_ACTOR_SUBS` on the service. Keep the client secret only where the CLI or MCP server runs.
{% endif %}- Leave `CORS_ORIGINS` unset on Render. The app then allows only its own `RENDER_EXTERNAL_URL`.
{% endif %}- Do not add CLI-only secrets to `render.yaml`. Render passes every service env var to the Docker build.
