{% endif %}{% if auth_provider == 'google' and include_backend %}The API checks each protected request in a fixed order. A request with an `Authorization` header must carry a valid agent key. A request without it must carry a valid session cookie, and a write must also send the CSRF token.

![How the API decides who you are: if sign-in settings are missing the API returns 503; if an Authorization header is present only a valid agent key passes; otherwise a valid session cookie is needed, and a write also needs a matching CSRF token.](docs/diagrams/auth-decision.svg)

{% endif %}{% if include_db %}The app starts with two tables. `user_profiles` has one row for each person. `items` is a sample table: replace it or add your own. The API takes `user_id` from sign-in, never from the request body, and each query filters by it.

![Starting data model: user_profiles has one row per person, keyed by user_id such as google:1234567890; items has many rows per person, linked by user_id.](docs/diagrams/data-model.svg)

{% endif %}{% if include_frontend and include_db %}On your computer, run the backend, the Vite dev server, and Postgres in Docker. Open the app at http://localhost:5173.

![Run an app on your computer: the browser opens the Vite dev server on port 5173, which forwards /api and /auth to FastAPI on port 8000, which uses Postgres in Docker on port 5432 and reads settings from the .env file.](docs/diagrams/local-dev-setup.svg)

